# HamZaban lexicon factory — research API keys (TEMPLATE, committed).
# Real values go in factory/.env (same names, NEVER committed — gitignored).
# Phases 2/3 (LLM merge/judge/topic refine) are fail-closed: missing keys => clean stop, no partial writes.
# Free-tier research only. Never reuse the bot runtime key (AI_API_KEY) for factory runs.
#
# Naming rule (provider-key-group convention): {PROVIDER}_API_KEY_{GROUP}
# with GROUP in G1/G2. The engine tries G1 first, then G2 (key rotation
# across groups on HTTP 429), then the legacy generic name. Fill G2 to
# get a rotation partner; a single populated group means 429 stops loud.
#
# Canonical grouped names (preferred — fill these):
# - AVALAI_API_KEY_G1 / AVALAI_API_KEY_G2 ..... AvalAI (https://api.avalai.ir/v1,
#   OpenAI-compatible) — paid chain: S2 judge glm-5.3-flash (wired);
#   S3 gemini-3.5-flash-lite + repair gemini-3.8-flash (follow-up).
#   Locked 2026-09-06 (model-chain-lock). Never committed.
# - OPENROUTER_API_KEY_G1 / OPENROUTER_API_KEY_G2 . OpenRouter — :free models fallback
# - GOOGLE_API_KEY_G1 / GOOGLE_API_KEY_G2 ..... Google direct (generativelanguage,
#   X-goog-api-key header) — gemini flash-lite fallback
# - GROQ_API_KEY_G1 / GROQ_API_KEY_G2 ......... Groq (https://api.groq.com/openai/v1,
#   OpenAI-compatible) — registry row
#
# Legacy generic names (still work as fallbacks — prefer the grouped names above):
# - AVALAI_API_KEY .......... legacy generic AvalAI (fallback after _G1/_G2)
# - OPENROUTER_API_KEY ...... legacy generic OpenRouter (fallback after _G1/_G2)
# - OPENROUTER_API_KEY_2 .... older numbered style (same slot as _G2; kept working)
# - GOOGLE_AI_API_KEY ....... legacy generic Google (fallback after _G1/_G2)
# - GROQ_API_KEY ............ legacy generic Groq (fallback after _G1/_G2)
# - OPENCODE_ZEN_API_KEY .... OpenCode Zen (https://opencode.ai/zen/v1) — muse-spark-1.3 primary
#   + spark-1.2/ling/mimo/nemotron fallback
#   (RETIRED from the precard run line — pipeline/run accept only
#   avalai|google; still read by archive/lexicon scripts, so the vars stay).
# - OPENCODE_ZEN_API_KEY_2 .. second Zen key for quota rotation (optional;
#   empty = single-key mode). Rotation stops with a clear message when all
#   keys 429 so the operator can switch servers; never committed.
#
# Secure key storage (WebUI operator keys):
# - AI_MASTER_KEY ........... Fernet master for keys pasted in the WebUI
#   (encrypted at rest in operator_keys.json). Empty = storage inactive
#   (fail-closed: pasted keys refuse to save and never persist). The WebUI
#   generates + stores it here on first use ONLY after you press the
#   activation button (operator-confirmed, never displayed). Real value
#   lives ONLY in this file (gitignored) — back it up; losing it makes
#   stored keys undecryptable. Generate by hand only if needed:
#     python -c "from cryptography.fernet import Fernet; print(Fernet.generate_key().decode())"
#
# Egress (canonical home: tools/egress/.env — same names; factory/.env is
# an accepted fallback, resolved through the same loader):
# - EGRESS_SUP_TOKEN ........ Loopback bearer for tools/egress/supervisor.py
#   (127.0.0.1:18789). factory/run shows it as set/unset and never prints
#   it. Real value lives in tools/egress/.env (same key name, gitignored);
#   export it into your shell before tunnel runs, e.g.:
#   foreach ($l in (Get-Content tools/egress/.env)) {
#     if ($l -match '^\s*([^#=\s][^=]*?)\s*=\s*(.*?)\s*$') {
#       [Environment]::SetEnvironmentVariable($matches[1].Trim(),
#         $matches[2], "Process") } }
# - EGRESS_SUP_URL .......... Supervisor base URL (default http://127.0.0.1:18789).
# - EGRESS_SUP_PORT ......... Supervisor port (default 18789; read by factory/run).
# - EGRESS_SUB_URL .......... single v2ray subscription (legacy; kept working).
# - EGRESS_SUB_URLS ......... MULTIPLE subscriptions: one per line OR comma
#   separated (both split; empties dropped).

AVALAI_API_KEY_G1=
AVALAI_API_KEY_G2=
AVALAI_API_KEY=
